                     /gene="birA"
                     /locus_tag="WEOB_035"
                     /function="Acts both as a biotin--[acetyl-CoA-carboxylase]
                     ligase and a biotin-operon repressor. In the presence of
                     ATP, BirA activates biotin to form the
                     BirA-biotinyl-5'-adenylate (BirA-bio-5'-AMP or holoBirA)
                     complex. HoloBirA can either transfer the biotinyl moiety
                     to the biotin carboxyl carrier protein (BCCP) subunit of
                     acetyl-CoA carboxylase, or bind to the biotin operator
                     site and inhibit transcription of the operon"
