     tmRNA           45808..46198
                     /gene="ssrA"
                     /locus_tag="WEOB_040"
                     /product="Transfer-messenger RNA"
                     /tag_peptide=45898..45939
                     /inference="profile:ARAGORN:1.2.36"
                     /inference="profile:RFAM:RF00023"
                     /function="The tmRNA forms a ribonucleoprotein complex
                     (tmRNP) together with Small Protein B (SmpB), Elongation
                     Factor Tu (EF-Tu), and ribosomal protein S1. In
                     trans-translation, tmRNA and its associated proteins bind
                     to bacterial ribosomes which have stalled in the middle of
                     protein biosynthesis, for example when reaching the end of
                     a messenger RNA which has lost its stop codon. The tmRNA
                     is remarkably versatile: it recycles the stalled ribosome,
                     adds a proteolysis-inducing tag to the unfinished
                     polypeptide, and facilitates the degradation of the
                     aberrant messenger RNA"
