                     /function="Part of the Sec protein translocase complex.
                     Interacts with the secYEG preprotein conducting channel.
                     Has a central role in coupling the hydrolysis of ATP to
                     the transfer of proteins into and across the cell
                     membrane, serving both as a receptor for the
                     preprotein-secB complex and as an ATP-driven molecular
                     motor driving the stepwise translocation of polypeptide
                     chains across the membrane"
