     CDS             complement(181105..182283)
                     /gene="ftsZ"
                     /locus_tag="WEOB_155"
                     /function="This protein is essential to the cell-division
                     process. It seems to assemble into a dynamic ring on the
                     inner surface of the cytoplasmic membrane at the place
                     where division will occur, and the formation of the ring
                     is the signal for septation to begin. Binds to and
                     hydrolyzes GTP. Involved in the synthesis of the septal
                     peptidoglycan"
