     CDS             432094..434184
                     /gene="clpB"
                     /locus_tag="WEOB_348"
                     /function="Part of a stress-induced multi-chaperone
                     system, it is involved in the recovery of the cell from
                     heat-induced damage, in cooperation with DnaK, DnaJ and
                     GrpE. Acts before DnaK, in the processing of protein
                     aggregates. Protein binding stimulates the ATPase
                     activity; ATP hydrolysis unfolds the denatured protein
                     aggregates, which probably helps expose new hydrophobic
                     binding sites on the surface of ClpB-bound aggregates,
                     contributing to the solubilization and refolding of
                     denatured protein aggregates by DnaK"
