                     /locus_tag="WEOB_360"
                     /function="Molecular chaperone that interacts specifically
                     with outer membrane proteins, thus maintaining the
                     solubility of early folding intermediates during passage
                     through the periplasm. Required for the efficient release
                     of OmpA from the inner membrane, the maintenance of its
                     solubility in the periplasm, and, in association with
                     lipopolysaccharide (LPS), for the efficient folding and
                     insertion of OmpA into the outer membrane"
