                     /EC_number="6.1.1.5"
                     /function="Catalyzes the attachment of isoleucine to
                     tRNA(Ile). As IleRS can inadvertently accommodate and
                     process structurally similar amino acids such as valine,
                     to avoid such errors it has two additional distinct
                     tRNA(Ile)-dependent editing activities. One activity is
                     designated as 'pretransfer' editing and involves the
                     hydrolysis of activated Val-AMP. The other activity is
                     designated 'posttransfer' editing and involves deacylation
                     of mischarged Val-tRNA(Ile)"
